   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d02_0204",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 76.0,
   "y": 2042.0,
   "width": 802.46,
   "height": 157.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "grp02_002"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1815482,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 21364742,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "- snet-agent has no NAT gateway and no default outbound access: the agent runtime has no internet\n  path. It reaches APIM through a private endpoint and the private MCP at its internal name.\n- Storage, Cosmos DB and AI Search accept no public traffic and no keys. The only way to data is a\n  private endpoint, with an on-behalf-of token.\n- All VNet egress leaves through one NAT address, the only address on the Key Vault firewall. The\n  APIM NSG allows three outbound destinations on 443; the jump-box NSG admits only Bastion and\n  denies the internet.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "- snet-agent has no NAT gateway and no default outbound access: the agent runtime has no internet\n  path. It reaches APIM through a private endpoint and the private MCP at its internal name.\n- Storage, Cosmos DB and AI Search accept no public traffic and no keys. The only way to data is a\n  private endpoint, with an on-behalf-of token.\n- All VNet egress leaves through one NAT address, the only address on the Key Vault firewall. The\n  APIM NSG allows three outbound destinations on 443; the jump-box NSG admits only Bastion and\n  denies the internet.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d02_0206",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 966.0,
   "y": 2009.0,
   "width": 134.48,
   "height": 25.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "grp02_003"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1831320,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 21574200,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Numbered flow",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "Numbered flow",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d02_0207",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 966.0,
   "y": 2042.0,
   "width": 658.91,
   "height": 140.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "grp02_003"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1839239,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 21678929,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. A client calls the APIM public gateway with a bearer token. Wall 1 (APIM) judges every call\n    there.\n2. The agent runtime has no internet path, so it reaches the same gateway through the APIM\n    private endpoint in snet-pe.\n3. APIM's backend calls leave through its outbound VNet integration in snet-apim.\n4. They stay inside the VNet to the MCP apps in the internal Container Apps environment\n    (NSG rule 110).",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "1. A client calls the APIM public gateway with a bearer token. Wall 1 (APIM) judges every call\n    there.\n2. The agent runtime has no internet path, so it reaches the same gateway through the APIM\n    private endpoint in snet-pe.\n3. APIM's backend calls leave through its outbound VNet integration in snet-apim.\n4. They stay inside the VNet to the MCP apps in the internal Container Apps environment\n    (NSG rule 110).",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d02_0208",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1659.0,
   "y": 2042.0,
   "width": 644.78,
   "height": 180.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "grp02_003"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1847158,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 21783658,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "5. The private MCP is called straight from the agent subnet at its internal name. It is never\n    behind APIM, so Wall 1 and the kill switch do not apply to it.\n6. After the on-behalf-of exchange, the MCP servers reach Storage, Cosmos DB and AI\n    Search through private endpoints. Private DNS answers with 10.42.1.x addresses.\n7. Public hosts (Entra, Azure Monitor, the vendor mock) are reached through the NAT\n    gateway's one static address, from snet-mcp, snet-apim and snet-jump only.\n8. The operator opens the VM in the Azure portal and connects through Bastion Developer.\n9. Bastion reaches the VM on RDP 3389, the only inbound NSG rule. From the VM the\n    private names resolve to the private endpoints.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "5. The private MCP is called straight from the agent subnet at its internal name. It is never\n    behind APIM, so Wall 1 and the kill switch do not apply to it.\n6. After the on-behalf-of exchange, the MCP servers reach Storage, Cosmos DB and AI\n    Search through private endpoints. Private DNS answers with 10.42.1.x addresses.\n7. Public hosts (Entra, Azure Monitor, the vendor mock) are reached through the NAT\n    gateway's one static address, from snet-mcp, snet-apim and snet-jump only.\n8. The operator opens the VM in the Azure portal and connects through Bastion Developer.\n9. Bastion reaches the VM on RDP 3389, the only inbound NSG rule. From the VM the\n    private names resolve to the private endpoints.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
